What was copied
---------------

Only the **data tables** (25 TSV files, ~4 KB). No Python source was copied.

The grammar's Python code was not copied because it is 1368 lines, of which
only 291 are pynini/FST; the remainder reads these same TSVs into dicts, which
`app/text/data.py` does in ~200 lines of standard-library Python. NeMo uses
finite-state transducers to emit *every* valid reading of an ambiguous input
(for audio-based normalization); a TTS frontend needs exactly one reading, so
the FST machinery and its 147 MB `pynini` dependency buy nothing here.

Modifications
-------------

None. The files are byte-identical to upstream. `app/text/data.py` reads them
directly; no table has been edited or extended.

